# A Luxel library scene — Apache-2.0. Grammar: library/README.md.
# `fit tile` as a COUNTER: the candle-stick sprite is an 8 px cell of two
# candles, so a tiled box's width sets how many burn — a zero `w` is the rest
# of the panel from x 1: eight candles on a 32-wide panel, sixteen on a 64,
# thirty-two on a 128. Behind them: a warm wash, a slow gold glitter (Twinkle
# ramped to one warm hue) drifting in the dark above. For Advent, Hanukkah,
# Diwali or a birthday.
# No `U` line on purpose: a wider panel lights MORE candles at the same 1:1
# size, not bigger ones. The shelves are grid rows too: a 32-row panel is one
# shelf of candles, a 64-row one a votive rack of two, and a 128-row one the
# same two shelves over an empty lower half.
# Menorah variant (on a 32x32): replace the two candle rows with
#   L sprite 1 18 16 12 normal 100 none tile 1    (four candles, left)
#   L sprite 13 14 8 12 normal 100 none fill 1     (the raised shamash; the
#                                                    cell's taller left candle)
#   L sprite 18 18 16 12 normal 100 none tile 1   (four candles, right)
# each with `I @spr/candle-stick`, and narrow the boxes to light night by night.
S - Candle Row
L color 0 0 0 0 normal 100 none fill 1
N Wash
K 140804
L pat 0 0 0 0 add 85 none fill 1
N Glitter
I @pat/twinkle
C sliderDensity 524288
C sliderFadeSeconds 196608
R 100 0:000000 255:ffcf7a
L sprite 1 18 0 12 normal 100 none tile 1
N Candles
I @spr/candle-stick
L sprite 1 48 0 12 normal 100 none tile 1
N Candles 2
I @spr/candle-stick
A 7
L color 0 30 0 2 normal 100 none fill 1
N Shelf
K 4a2a14
L color 0 60 0 2 normal 100 none fill 1
N Shelf 2
K 4a2a14
